WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.530
Organisms with supernatural powers are always
fascinating!

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.670
But they are no more
restricted to fiction stories.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:16.640
They are a part of our practical scientific
world!

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.640
Yes!

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:23.790
Imagine a mice glowing in the dark, or a plant
that fights its deadliest predator!

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.200
These are not just thoughts, but successful
experiments!

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.009
Today, all thanks to
Biotechnology, we have several products with

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:37.790
wide applications in the fields of
agriculture, environment, healthcare and many

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.410
more.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.090
And what kind of Products are we talking about?

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:46.490
Well, in this video, we will
mainly be discussing about the transgenic

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:52.800
organisms, also known as Genetically
Modified organisms, and abbreviated as GMOs.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:59.670
And what do we mean by
transgenic or Genetically Modified Organisms?

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:05.470
Well, an organism which contains DNA from
another organism integrated into its

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:10.500
genomic DNA is called Transgenic organism.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.999
So will transgenic organisms be
different from their original parental forms?

00:01:15.999 --> 00:01:18.130
Of course yes!

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:23.249
A mice will not usually
glow in the dark, but when we manipulate it’s

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:28.290
genes, then the transgenic mice
obtained shows the unusual ability to glow

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:29.779
in the dark brightly!

00:01:29.779 --> 00:01:34.729
Let us get introduced to these examples one
by one.

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:40.130
To begin with, we have the
cotton plant named “Bt cotton”

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.429
And what does this “BT” mean?

00:01:42.429 --> 00:01:44.759
Does it stand for “Biotechnology”?

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:46.329
Nope!

00:01:46.329 --> 00:01:51.399
The
prefix “BT” stands for “Bacillus thuringiensis”,

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:54.520
the bacteria which comes to the
rescue of Cotton plants!

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:58.859
Bt → Bacillus thuringiensis
Have you come across the phrase “The Enemy

00:01:58.859 --> 00:02:01.880
of my enemy is my friend?”

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.599
Well, that is exactly the case we are going
to glance at!

00:02:06.599 --> 00:02:11.060
Cotton plants have the biggest enemies in
the form of insects.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.990
And there are
certain bacteria, like Bacillus thuringiensis,

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:17.330
which are like the enemies of these
insects.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:22.160
They are actually capable of producing certain
toxins that can kill these

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.230
insects.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:28.500
Thus, for the cotton plant, their “enemy’s
enemy”, which is the bacterium

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.520
is like a “friend”.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.420
And this relation is exploited by genetic
engineers to get cotton

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.420
modified!

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.590
Let us find out how!

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.700
The first thing we need to know is about the
protein, and then, about the “gene”

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.160
which creates the magic!

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:49.250
These bacteria produce certain proteins, which
are capable of killing various

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:54.600
insects like cotton bollworms, beetles and
others.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.150
These proteins are also called
toxins.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:03.000
The genes encoding the toxins is called “cry”
gene.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.120
And don’t these toxins
harm the bacterial cell?

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.390
Nope!

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.270
Inside the bacterial cells, these toxins are
present

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:14.650
in the form of crystals which are inactive
by nature.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:19.920
The crystals get activated only
when in contact with apt pH conditions, found

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.920
in the gut of insects!

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.121
Crystals get activated → Apt pH conditions
Hence, the toxins are harmful only to the

00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:28.500
insects and not the bacterial cells!

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.350
Now what we do is take the “cry” gene
from the bacterium and insert it into the

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:38.300
cotton plant through one of the various methods
of gene transfer.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.300
And once

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.500
inside the cotton plant, the gene gives rise
to proteins, which are present in the

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:47.360
inactive crystalised forms in the plant as
well.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:52.010
These when consumed by the
insects, get activated inside their gut, creating

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:57.040
holes in the lining and eventually
killing the organism.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:01.790
This is how cotton plants get the ability
to naturally fight the threats and get

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.850
benefited.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:08.930
In this way, transgenic plants can be created
using genetic engineering.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.400
Various
other useful plants that have better resistance

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:19.040
capacity, or which have high yield,
can be designed using such techniques.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:25.259
Several important and beneficial traits can
thus be incorporated in plants.

00:04:25.259 --> 00:04:27.169
And what about animals?

00:04:27.169 --> 00:04:31.330
Well, transgenic animals are also a boon to
researchers.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:37.430
Let us learn about an interesting transgenic
animal in the next video!

